# p_census_peak_s5: diagnostic. Owner census at the true peak of the published line.
#
# defect     the census inherits PEAK_TRIGGER_PCT (2%); on a plateau the last census lands below the peak
#            (s6_plaintext_free_early_trim run2: census at 293,740 / 1,003,688 / 1,545,736 kB, peak
#            2,073,824: 74.5%). Run with PEAK_TRIGGER_PCT=0 (every new maximum signals a census).
# question   published line ends at s5_embed_chunk; two level humps per replicate:
#              conversion  2,048,432 / 2,055,244 / 2,061,096
#              inference   2,047,080 / 2,072,904 / 2,053,316
#            conversion hump = ONNX parse working set (~1.5 GB; plaintext_free_early_cpu released 433 MB
#            with and without malloc_trim(0), no move). Inference hump never censused (p_census_owner_s1..s4
#            fired during conversion).
# not a step probe_census_cpu records only; the five s5 levers unchanged.
SHAFT_LEVERS=plaintext_free_cpu,triple_share_free_cpu,trace_nograd_cpu,onnx_single_file_export_cpu,encrypt_spill_cpu,embed_chunk_cpu,probe_census_cpu
SHAFT_INNER_ENV="SHAFT_EMBED_CHUNKS=16"
